1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,657
I love parades.

2
00:00:00,657 --> 00:00:05,864
The Thanksgiving Day parade is always such great fun.

3
00:00:05,864 --> 00:00:09,255
Look at that Superman balloon!

4
00:00:09,255 --> 00:00:15,986
Wowee! Just floating along high above Central Park West.

5
00:00:15,986 --> 00:00:18,385
Don't you just love it?

6
00:00:18,385 --> 00:00:21,338
Oh, and the bands and the music.

7
00:00:21,338 --> 00:00:22,674
John Philip Sousa.

8
00:00:22,674 --> 00:00:24,490
I love his music.

9
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:32,086
Da dada da da dada da da da da da da dada.

10
00:00:32,086 --> 00:00:36,374
Oh, look at that float, Robbie.

11
00:00:36,374 --> 00:00:38,910
Look at those funny-looking clowns.

12
00:00:38,910 --> 00:00:41,331
It's for kids.

13
00:00:41,331 --> 00:00:45,473
Maybe so, but parades always make me feel like a kid.

14
00:00:45,473 --> 00:00:48,927
Remember when you and your dad and I

15
00:00:48,927 --> 00:00:52,934
went to the Thanksgiving Day parade?

16
00:00:52,934 --> 00:01:01,156
You were four or five years old, I think.

17
00:01:01,156 --> 00:01:05,090
Hello, hello.... Oh, hi, Susan.

18
00:01:05,090 --> 00:01:11,382
How are you?... Here's Mom.

19
00:01:11,382 --> 00:01:13,521
Hello, Susan.

20
00:01:13,521 --> 00:01:17,403
Yes, he missed a phone call from Alexandra.

21
00:01:17,403 --> 00:01:19,990
Yes, I know, but he'll get over it.

22
00:01:19,990 --> 00:01:22,881
Good. Then you'll be here about five?

23
00:01:22,881 --> 00:01:24,363
Oh, fine.

24
00:01:24,363 --> 00:01:28,515
I look forward to seeing you and Harry and Michelle.

25
00:01:28,515 --> 00:01:30,279
Drive carefully.

26
00:01:30,279 --> 00:01:32,522
Good-bye.

27
00:01:32,522 --> 00:01:33,670
Taste Ellen's turkey dressing.

28
00:01:33,670 --> 00:01:36,300
It's delicious.

29
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:37,646
I'm not surprised.

30
00:01:37,646 --> 00:01:39,357
It's Grandma's recipe.

31
00:01:39,357 --> 00:01:41,152
It's my favorite part of the meal.

32
00:01:41,152 --> 00:01:43,729
What about my famous apple pie?

33
00:01:43,729 --> 00:01:48,007
Dad, your apple pie is my favorite dessert.

34
00:01:48,007 --> 00:01:49,196
How's the parade?

35
00:01:49,196 --> 00:02:00,643
OK.

36
00:02:00,643 --> 00:02:03,095
Mom! Is it for me?

37
00:02:03,095 --> 00:02:04,577
No, Robbie.

38
00:02:04,577 --> 00:02:06,945
Who was it?

39
00:02:06,945 --> 00:02:08,667
Wrong number.

40
00:02:08,667 --> 00:02:11,004
Philip, would you join me in the kitchen, please?

41
00:02:11,004 --> 00:02:11,735
It's getting late.

42
00:02:11,735 --> 00:02:13,634
We have vegetables to prepare.

43
00:02:13,634 --> 00:02:14,636
Can I help with anything?

44
00:02:14,636 --> 00:02:15,230
No, honey.

45
00:02:15,230 --> 00:02:16,691
You just relax with Grandpa.

46
00:02:16,691 --> 00:02:20,469
I'll get you to help serve later.

47
00:02:20,469 --> 00:02:23,463
Ellen reminds me so much of Grandma.

48
00:02:23,463 --> 00:02:25,571
What time does the Michigan football game come on?

49
00:02:25,571 --> 00:02:26,281
Four.

50
00:02:26,281 --> 00:02:28,305
Philip!

51
00:02:28,305 --> 00:02:32,343
I'll be back to see the game.

52
00:02:32,343 --> 00:02:36,569
Grandpa, when did Dad graduate from Michigan?

53
00:02:36,569 --> 00:02:38,416
Let me think.

54
00:02:38,416 --> 00:02:42,224
He graduated from medical school in 1960

55
00:02:42,224 --> 00:02:47,254
and from the University of Michigan in 1956.

56
00:02:47,254 --> 00:02:48,683
Did you go to Michigan, too, Grandpa?

57
00:02:48,683 --> 00:02:53,264
Yup. I graduated in 1937.

58
00:02:53,264 --> 00:02:53,264
I've got to start thinking about college soon.
